    "summary": "I built one planter cell with a water pipe coming up through its floor. It's a single full-depth base cell at q0 r0. A vertical riser (riser:0,0,0) comes up through the floor, and in the cell sits a full-depth drained bin made for the pipe, with a PVC bore for it to pass through (hex-bin-full-drain-pvc). I filled the bin with soil and planted it. I also capped the six side faces with solid end caps and locked the joints. The build has 8 parts, about 559 g of filament and an estimated 779 minutes of printing. The configurator's checks found no rule issues and no parts colliding. It only checks fit, though, so it can't tell whether the plastic will be watertight or stand up to water and sun.",
